# UI components

Edit-time standards for `packages/ui/src/components/{primitives,blocks,templates}/`. Contract: [UI.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI.md). Workflow: **`$components-authoring`**.

**Scope:** `*.tsx`, `*.types.ts`, `*.variants.ts` — not `packages/ui/test/**` ([testing.mdc](./testing.mdc)).

**Precedence:** Variants, token classes, and registry install surfaces → **this rule** over [typescript.mdc](./typescript.mdc) and [code-commenting.mdc](./code-commenting.mdc).

---

## Three-file shape

| File | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| `ComponentName.tsx` | Render, `displayName`, React 19 `ref` prop, single `export { … }` at bottom |
| `ComponentName.types.ts` | Public props; `ref?: React.Ref<…>` when ref-capable |
| `ComponentName.variants.ts` | Visual classes only |

Compound components (Sidebar, Menu, …): multiple sub-components in one `.tsx`, one bottom export block.

---

## Do not

- Use `cva()` in **blocks** or **templates**.
- Use raw Tailwind palette in `*.variants.ts` (`bg-blue-500`, `text-gray-*`, …).
- Edit `packages/registry/templates/` directly.
- Expose Base UI types through the public component API.
- Concatenate class strings — use `cn()` or `mergeClassName()` (see below).

---

## Variant pattern

| Layer | Pattern |
| ----- | ------- |
| Primitives | **Variant grid** → `export const fooVariants = cva(…)`. **Static parts** of compound primitives may use `*Classes` string exports (e.g. Slider, Table sub-parts). |
| Blocks / templates | `export const fooClasses = (…) => "…"` or `(): string =>` — **never** `cva()`. Compose with `cn()` in `.tsx`. |

See [UI_VARIANTS.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI_VARIANTS.md), [UI_AUDIT.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI_AUDIT.md).

---

## Tokens in `*.variants.ts`

Use `--lex-*` only (from `cssVarPrefix` in [generator.config.ts](../../packages/tokens/src/generators/generator.config.ts)):

- Tailwind v4 arbitrary: `bg-(--lex-button-primary-background)`, `rounded-(--lex-button-radius)`
- CSS vars in strings: `var(--lex-color-background-subtle)`, `var(--lex-space-4)`
- Block layout BEM: `lex-sidebar__nav` is OK when paired with token vars

No raw palette. `ui:check` runs token audit.

---

## className

| Surface | Merge |
| ------- | ----- |
| **Base UI** primitive wrappers | `className={mergeClassName(variantFn(…), className)}` — `mergeClassName` returns the callback Base UI expects |
| **Native HTML**, blocks, templates | `className={cn(…Classes(), className)}` |

Do not use `forwardRef` — codebase uses **ref prop** only.

---

## Exports and install surface

- **Consumer install:** registry-first — `lexsys add`, not deep imports from `@dalexto/lexsys-ui` blocks in app code.
- **`packages/ui/src/index.ts`:** reference package for monorepo/playground; today exports primitives **and** pilot blocks/template. Do not add exports without [UI_CATALOG.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI_CATALOG.md) + [REGISTRY.md](../../docs/reference/registry/REGISTRY.md) alignment.

Composition rules (e.g. Sidebar nav items use plain `<a>` / `<button>`, not `Button`): [UI.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI.md), [UI_COMPOSITION.md](../../docs/reference/ui/UI_COMPOSITION.md).

---

## Registry (two-zone — current behavior)

```txt
packages/ui/src/components/     ← edit source
packages/registry/templates/    ← generated on registry:sync — never edit
packages/registry/src/items/    ← install metadata — see below
```

| Artifact | `pnpm registry:sync` today |
| -------- | --------------------------- |
| `templates/**` | Regenerated from UI source (overwrite when changed) |
| `src/items/*.ts` (primitives) | **Scaffold only if file missing** — sync does **not** overwrite existing items |
| `src/items/*.ts` (blocks/templates) | **Manual** — sync does not create or update item files yet |

After install-affecting UI edits: tell user to run **`$registry-sync`** / `pnpm registry:sync` and review item metadata (`registryDependencies`, `files`, version). Full auto item sync is planned — [REVIEW_TODO.md](../../docs/REVIEW_TODO.md) (SI.4–SI.5).

---

## After edit (agent)

Do **not** run `pnpm ui:check`, `registry:sync`, or tests unless the user asks. Install-affecting change → user runs gates or **`$components-authoring`** / **`$registry-sync`**; test edits → [testing.mdc](./testing.mdc) notify pattern.

